  "name": "room_schroeder_octaves",
  "description": "An impulse response (two exponential decays, a direct sound, background noise) through IEC 61260-1 octave-band Butterworth filters (order 3) run backwards in time; Schroeder integral from each band's -20 dB trigger to a fixed truncation point without correction; EDT/T20/T30 by numpy.polyfit over 0..-10, -5..-25, -5..-35 dB; C50/C80 by window-before-filtering from the broadband trigger.",
